ENTRY            20274   20251214   20260826   20260826       2323
SUBENT        20274001   20251214   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  9         17
TITLE      Fission of Am241 induced by thermal neutrons
AUTHOR     (M.Hyakutake)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNKYU)
REFERENCE  (J,TRKU,39,170,1966)
FACILITY   (REAC,2JPNKTO) KUR
INC-SOURCE (THCOL) graphite thermal neutron column
SAMPLE     Am241 (77+/-3 ug/cm2) and U235 (215+/-3 ug),
            1 cm x 1 cm evaporated onto Al (0.1 mm),
           The thickness of Am241 and U235 was determined by
            alpha counting
DETECTOR   (SOLST) 2.2 cm and 2.3 cm from the target centre
            and perpendicular to the beam line
HISTORY    (19711010C)
           (19740626E)
           (19840106U) A.P.T. Japan code changed to JPN
           (19840106E)
           (20251214A) On. Recompiled. 003 added.
ENDBIB              17
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           20
SUBENT        20274002   20251214   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  6          9
REACTION   (95-AM-241(N,F),,SIG,,MXW)
MONITOR    (92-U-235(N,F),,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (,D.J.Hughes+,R,BNL-325,(2),1958)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Statistics, mainly in Am241 target thickness
            determination
STATUS     (TABLE,,M.Hyakutake,J,TRKU,39,170,1966) Table 2
HISTORY    (19860808A) HH MXW inserted
           (19860822E)
           (20251214A) On. MONIT(-ERR) added.
ENDBIB               9
NOCOMMON             0          0
DATA                 5          1
EN-DUMMY   DATA       ERR-S      MONIT      MONIT-ERR
EV         B          B          B          B
 0.0253     3.8        0.2        582.       4.
ENDDATA              3
ENDSUBENT           17
SUBENT        20274003   20251214   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  8         15
REACTION  1(95-AM-241(N,F),PRE,AKE,HF,MXW)
          2(95-AM-241(N,F),PRE,AKE,LF,MXW)
ANALYSIS   E(pre) = E(sec) + nu-bar * E(sec)/(242 - nu-bar)
ASSUMED    (ASSUM,95-AM-241(N,F),,NU)
REL-REF    (R,40400002,V.I.Levedev+,J,JNE,10,90,1959)
            nu-bar=3.14+/-0.05
ADD-RES    The mean energies derived from the compiled
            most probable energies are
           . <EH> =  77.8 +/- 3.6 MeV
           . <EL> = 108.2 +/- 3.3 MeV
           . <TKE>= 186.0 +/- 4.9 MeV
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on sources of uncertainty
STATUS     (TABLE,,M.Hyakutake,J,TRKU,39,170,1966)
            Text (p.173)
HISTORY    (20251214C) On
ENDBIB              15
COMMON               3          3
EN-DUMMY   ASSUM      ASSUM-ERR
EV         PRT/FIS    PRT/FIS
